Provenance caveat (design lineage)
----------------------------------
The design lineage of this decoder runs through the GitHub repository jday96314/QuantumAI:
- That repository states no licence. Every public note on it says it "states no license"
  (SomeJoint's notebook versions 13 to 21, Ahmed Berat Ozer's DQI_NOTICE.md, Alex Chilton's
  notebook).
- It returned HTTP 404 on 2026-10-29 (api.github.com/repos/jday96314/QuantumAI and
  github.com/jday96314/QuantumAI), so its content can no longer be checked.
- Alex Chilton's 883-qubit decoder, the design this code starts from, was by his own account
  rebuilt from that repository's code: "The decoder is jday96314's ... Rebuilt it from their
  code" (Chilton's portfolio notebook, cell 9).
- SomeJoint describes its own decoder as "rebuilt from scratch", from a design that "starts
  from" Chilton's 883-qubit Schur decoder (SomeJoint notebook versions 10 to 12), and licenses
  its notebook code as Apache-2.0.
So the code ported here carries a clear Apache-2.0 grant from its author, while its design
lineage passes through unlicensed code that another author reused. We could not compare the
ported text with jday96314's code, because the repository is gone.

What is whose
-------------
The circuit design, and every file under pro_q2_897/, is SomeJoint's and its credited
contributors' work (above), not ours. A circuit built from this directory is a reproduction
of SomeJoint's 897-qubit decoder. Any change we make to the design will live outside
pro_q2_897/, and its effect will be measured against this ported baseline.

Our modifications
-----------------
None of the ported files was changed. Our additions are exactly these three files:
- generate.py: our launcher. It re-implements the upstream build script
  pro_q2_897/build_897.py (which we do not run) with the same register layout and output
  format, and adds a SHA-256 check of every kit file against MANIFEST.json and a JSON build
  record.
- MANIFEST.json: the SHA-256 of every ported file.
- .gitattributes: turns off line-ending conversion so checkouts stay byte-identical.
LICENSE (the upstream Apache-2.0 text, unchanged) and this NOTICE are attribution files,
not modifications.

kickmix (the circuit builder the code runs on) is Google's, under its own licence; it is
not part of this directory.
